  "question": "Let X be a random variable taking values 0, 1, 2, 3 with $P(X=k)=k/(6)$ for k=0,1,2,3. <br /><br />(a) Find the mean and variance of X.<br /><br />(b) Find the probability that X is at least 2.<br /><br />(c) For what value of t does $P(X<t)\\geq 0.7$?",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Values: k=0,1,2,3; P(X=0)=0; P(1)=1/6, P(2)=2/6, P(3)=3/6<br /><br />(a) Mean:<br />$E(X)=1\\times1/6+2\\times1/3+3\\times1/2=1/6+2/3+3/2=(1+4+9)/6=14/6=7/3$<br />$E(X^2)=1^2\\times1/6+2^2\\times1/3+3^2\\times1/2=1/6+4/3+9/2=(1+8+27)/6=36/6=6$<br />Variance: $6-(7/3)^2=6-49/9= (54-49)/9=5/9$<br /><br />(b) $P(X\\geq2)=P(2)+P(3)=1/3+1/2=5/6$<br /><br />(c) $P(X<t)\\geq0.7$<br />$P(X<3)=P(0)+P(1)+P(2)=0+1/6+1/3=1/2$<br />$P(X<4)=1$<br />So for $t\\geq 4$, $P(X<4)=1\\geq0.7$; but for t=3, $P=1/2<0.7$<br />So $t=4$<br /><br />Final answers:<br />(a) Mean $7/3$, variance $5/9$<br />(b) $5/6$<br />(c) $t=4$",
  "explanation_image": [],
